# Ace PHP MVC Framework — Cursor AI Rules
# Read GUIDE.md for the full architecture reference.

You are working on a PHP MVC application built with the Ace Framework.

Architecture: MVC + Service Layer + Repository Pattern.
Namespace: Core = Ace\, Application = App\.
PHP version: >= 8.2.

MANDATORY RULES:
1. Controllers NEVER contain business logic or database queries. They only orchestrate.
2. Services contain business logic. They call Repositories, never the database directly.
3. Repositories contain all database queries. They use Models.
4. All user input MUST be validated before reaching Services. Use $this->validate() or FormRequest classes.
5. The standard data flow is: Controller → Validate → Service → Repository → Model.
6. Views use Blade-like template syntax: {{ }}, @if, @foreach, @extends, @section, @csrf, @error, @paginate, @tailwind, @bootstrap, @css.
7. Zero npm required for CSS: use @tailwind or @bootstrap, or extend layouts/tailwind or layouts/bootstrap.
8. When creating any feature, generate: Migration, Model, Repository, Service, FormRequest, Controller, Routes, and Views.

Naming: UserController, UserService, UserRepository, StoreUserRequest, User (model).
File paths: app/Controllers/, app/Services/, app/Repositories/, app/Requests/, app/Models/, views/.
Routes: routes/web.php (web), routes/api.php (API first with CORS and API keys).
CLI: php ace make:controller|model|service|repository|request|layout|apikey|middleware|migration|seeder <Name>.
API Auth: Authorization: Bearer <key> or X-Api-Key: <key>. Generate keys with php ace make:apikey <Name>.

Full documentation: GUIDE.md
